IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 2133 of 2020
CITATION: (2021) 15 SCC 125
YEAR: 2021

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: D.Y. Chandrachud, M.R. Shah

PARTIES:
Lt. Col. Nitisha vs Union of India

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Constitution of India

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Article 14, Article 15

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
indirect discrimination, substantive equality, medical fitness criteria for women

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Formulated the legal framework for indirect discrimination under Indian constitutional law, holding that facially neutral evaluation benchmarks causing disproportionate impact violate Article 14.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Article 14, Article 15.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

